/* pkpm-remap-flux.mac ------------------------------------------------------------
   Kernels of the exact-remap configuration-space face flux of the eight PKPM blocks
   X = [F, G, M0_perp (x, y, z), N_perp (x, y, z)] (gkyl_dg_pkpm_remap_flux_surf). The transverse
   node count is a run-time input, so nothing here depends on it: the kernels work in the
   orthonormal modal basis of the face,

     psi_a(transverse) phi_m(w),  phi = [1/sqrt(2), sqrt(3/2) w, sqrt(5/2) (3 w^2 - 1)/2],

   with psi_a the products over the transverse directions (ascending) of [1/sqrt(2), sqrt(3/2) s],
   a = bit 0 for the first transverse direction and bit 1 for the second (psi_0 = 1 in 1x).

   pkpm_remap_flux_trace_<dir>_<c>x1v_ser_p1(jdinv_l, jdinv_r, f_l, f_r, G_l, G_r)
     The traces of the eight blocks of one velocity cell on both sides of a face of direction dir,
     G_s[c*NT + a*3 + m] = int psi_a phi_m X_c(trace), the left cell at its upper edge and the
     right cell at its lower edge, each scaled by 1/J_dir of its cell: the blocks are stored
     Jacobian-weighted, and the flux needs (J X)/J_dir, as the face Jacobian J/J_dir times the
     physical trace.

   pkpm_remap_flux_store_<dir>_<c>x1v_ser_p1(wpsi, proj, flux)
     Accumulate into the stored surface modes of one side of the face the Legendre projections
     proj[m*8 + c] of the eight blocks at one transverse node:
     flux[c*NK + k(a, m)] += wpsi[a] proj[m*8 + c]/coef_k, where wpsi[a] = (weight of the node)
     psi_a(node) and coef_k the factor of the surface mode in the factorized basis.

   pkpm_remap_flux_interval_<dir>_1v_p2(fc, w_lo, w_up, side_l, side_r, cell_l, cell_r, Y_l, Y_r,
                                        P_l, P_r, mom, share)
     One interval [w_lo, w_up] of the velocity supermesh of a transverse node of a face of
     direction dir, in the face-frame label wbar. On it each side s is in one velocity cell, where
     its eight blocks in the face frame are X_s = Y_s[c] + Y_s[8 + c] eta_s + Y_s[16 + c] (3 eta_s^2 - 1),
     eta_s = cell_s[0] + cell_s[1] wbar the cell coordinate of the side. The kernel adds the
     3-point Gauss-Legendre quadrature over the interval (exact: the flux is at most cubic between
     the kinks of its HLL weights, which are ends of intervals) of
       P_s[m*8 + c]: the flux pkpm_harm_conf_flux (gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h) against the Legendre
                     mode m of the cell of side s, int phi_m(eta_s) flux_c d eta_s;
       mom:          the face-frame moments [M0, M1, M2 of F, M0 of G, M0 of M0_perp (3)] of the flux;
       share:        the flux weighted for the blend, per receiving side: |w_s F| (momentum) and
                     w_s^2 |F| + 2 |G| (energy) of the flux in the frame of side s, w_s = r wbar + c,
                     in total and, times cell_s[2], outside the grid of the side.
     A side outside its velocity grid passes Y_s = 0 and cell_s = [0, 0, 1] (with any P_s, which
     then receives zero); a side inside passes cell_s[2] = 0. The kernel does not depend on the
     configuration-space dimension: it sees one transverse node.

   pkpm_remap_flux_to_face_<c>x1v_ser_p1(psi, fwd, G, X, Y)
     One velocity cell of one side at a transverse node: the blocks of the modal traces G
     (pkpm_remap_flux_trace_*) at the node as Legendre coefficients in w, X[m*8 + c] of
     [1, eta, 3 eta^2 - 1], in the frame of the side, and the same in the face frame, Y, by the
     change of frame with the factors fwd (pkpm_harm_frame_change, gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h).

   pkpm_remap_flux_from_face_<dir>_<c>x1v_ser_p1(wpsi, bck, P, flux)
     One velocity cell of one side at a transverse node: the projection P of the face-frame flux
     (pkpm_remap_flux_interval_*) taken back to the frame of the side with the factors bck and
     accumulated into the stored surface modes as pkpm_remap_flux_store_* does.

   pkpm_remap_flux_label_<dir>_1v_p2(fc, w_center, dw, X_l, X_r, proj, mom_l, mom_r, speed)
     The label-paired flux of one velocity cell at a transverse node of a face of direction dir:
     the flux pkpm_harm_conf_flux of the two sides paired at equal w, each in its own frame (X_l,
     X_r of pkpm_remap_flux_to_face_*), at the 3 Gauss-Legendre points of the cell. proj[m*8 + c]
     is its projection on the Legendre modes of the cell (the same for both sides, overwritten)
     and mom_l, mom_r accumulate the moments [M0, M1, M2 of F, M0 of G, M0 of M0_perp (3)] in w of
     the contribution of each side. speed is raised to the speed bounds of the flux at the points
     (the fastest signal in either direction and the spread of the two bounds), from which the
     updater forms the rates of the face. The kernel does not depend on the configuration-space
     dimension. */
load("core/modal-basis.mac")$
load("util_maxima/out-scripts.mac")$
load("core/nodal_operations/nodal_functions.mac")$
load("vlasov/vlasov/vlasov-basis.mac")$
load("vlasov/vlasov/nodal-lax-emit.mac")$
load("vlasov/vlasov/nodal-hll-emit.mac")$
load("vlasov/vlasov/surf-eval-tables.mac")$
load("pkpm/pkpm/pkpm-flux-tables.mac")$
load(stringproc)$
fpprec : 24$

/* The orthonormal face modes: [psi list, phi list, flat list psi_a phi_m in the order a*3 + m]. */
pkpmRemapFluxModes(surfCVars, vv) := block([modes, old, i, j, a, m, phi],
  modes : [1],
  for i : 1 thru length(surfCVars) do (
    old : modes,
    modes : append(makelist(old[j]/sqrt(2), j, 1, length(old)),
                   makelist(old[j]*sqrt(3/2)*surfCVars[i], j, 1, length(old)))
  ),
  phi : [1/sqrt(2), sqrt(3/2)*vv, sqrt(5/2)*(3*vv^2 - 1)/2],
  [modes, phi, flatten(makelist(makelist(modes[a]*phi[m], m, 1, 3), a, 1, length(modes)))]
)$

calcPKPMRemapFluxTrace(dir, fh, funcNm, cdim) := block(
  [lb, pkC, pkV, pkbP, NP, cv, surfCVars, vv, md, tr, NT, ipVars, gl, gr, k],
  lb : loadPKPMPhaseBasis(cdim),
  pkC : copylist(lb[1]), pkV : copylist(lb[3]), pkbP : copylist(lb[6]),
  NP : length(pkbP), cv : pkC[dir], surfCVars : delete(cv, pkC), vv : pkV[1],
  md : pkpmRemapFluxModes(surfCVars, vv), tr : md[3], NT : length(tr),
  ipVars : append(surfCVars, [vv]),
  gl : calcInnerProdList(ipVars, 1, tr, subst(cv = 1, doExpand1(fl, pkbP))),
  gr : calcInnerProdList(ipVars, 1, tr, subst(cv = -1, doExpand1(fr, pkbP))),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_remap_flux_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH void ~a(double jdinv_l, double jdinv_r, const double *f_l, const double *f_r,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT G_l, double* GKYL_RESTRICT G_r) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // jdinv_l/r: 1/J_~a of the left/right cell (J_~a: position-map Jacobian of direction ~a). ~%", cv, cv, cv),
  printf(fh, "  // f_l/f_r:   Jacobian-weighted blocks J [F, G, M0_perp, N_perp] of one velocity cell in the left/right cell. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // G_l/G_r:   Output modal traces of the eight blocks on the face of direction ~a: ~%", cv),
  printf(fh, "  //            G[c*~a + a*3 + m], a transverse mode, m Legendre mode in w. ~%", NT),
  printf(fh, "  for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    const double *fl = &f_l[c*~a], *fr = &f_r[c*~a]; ~%", NP, NP),
  printf(fh, "    double *gl = &G_l[c*~a], *gr = &G_r[c*~a]; ~%", NT, NT),
  for k : 1 thru NT do
    printf(fh, "    gl[~a] = jdinv_l*(~a); ~%", k-1, float(expand(gl[k]))),
  for k : 1 thru NT do
    printf(fh, "    gr[~a] = jdinv_r*(~a); ~%", k-1, float(expand(gr[k]))),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$

calcPKPMRemapFluxStore(dir, fh, funcNm, cdim) := block(
  [lb, pkC, pkV, pkP, cv, surfCVars, vv, md, tr, bSurf, NK, ipVars, ip, idx, k, a, m, fact],
  lb : loadPKPMPhaseBasis(cdim),
  pkC : copylist(lb[1]), pkV : copylist(lb[3]), pkP : copylist(lb[5]),
  cv : pkC[dir], surfCVars : delete(cv, pkC), vv : pkV[1],
  md : pkpmRemapFluxModes(surfCVars, vv), tr : md[3],
  bSurf : basisFromVars("tenhyb", delete(cv, pkP), 1),
  NK : length(bSurf),
  if NK # length(tr) then error("calcPKPMRemapFluxStore: surface basis size mismatch"),
  ipVars : append(surfCVars, [vv]),
  fact : laxFactorizeBasis(bSurf, if cdim > 1 then surfCVars else [prjdummy], pkV),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_remap_flux_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH void ~a(const double *wpsi, const double *proj, double* GKYL_RESTRICT flux) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // wpsi:  Weight of the transverse node times the transverse modes at the node. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // proj:  Legendre projections in w of the eight blocks at the node: proj[m*8 + c]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // flux:  Accumulated surface modes of one side of the face: flux[c*~a + k]. ~%", NK),
  printf(fh, "  for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    double *out = &flux[c*~a]; ~%", NK),
  for k : 1 thru NK do (
    ip : calcInnerProdList(ipVars, 1, tr, bSurf[k]),
    idx : sublist_indices(ip, lambda([z], is(abs(float(z) - 1.0) < 1.0e-12))),
    if length(idx) # 1 then error("calcPKPMRemapFluxStore: surface mode is not a face mode"),
    a : floor((idx[1] - 1)/3), m : (idx[1] - 1) - 3*a,
    /* The stored modes are the integrals of the flux against the normalized shapes of the
       factorized surface basis (b_k = coef_k chi psi; laxFactorizeBasis), not the orthonormal
       coefficients, so the store divides by coef_k. */
    printf(fh, "    out[~a] += ~a*wpsi[~a]*proj[~a + c]; ~%", k-1, float(1/fact[3][k]), a, m*8)
  ),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$

/* Slots of the per-side inputs and of the shares of the interval kernels, written into the
   header by the driver: the single definition read by the kernels and by the updater. */
pkpmRemapFluxSlots : [
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_R", 0, "r: w_s = r wbar + c takes the face-frame label to the label of the side"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_C", 1, "c, the part of the shift along the field direction of the face"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_KINV", 2, "density factor of the map from the face frame back to the side"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_EG", 3, "K_inv/r_inv^2, the factor of the block G mapped back to the side"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_CC", 4, "|c_perp_inv|^2"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_CPERP", 5, "first of the three components of c_perp_inv"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SIDE_NUM", 8, "size of side_l/side_r"],
  ["PKPM_RF_CELL_ETA0", 0, "eta_s = ETA0 + ETA1 wbar: cell coordinate of the side at the label wbar"],
  ["PKPM_RF_CELL_ETA1", 1, "2 r/dw of the velocity cell"],
  ["PKPM_RF_CELL_OUT", 2, "1 if the side is outside its velocity grid on the interval, else 0"],
  ["PKPM_RF_CELL_NUM", 3, "size of cell_l/cell_r"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SHARE_MOM_OUT", 0, "momentum share outside the grid of side s, at MOM_OUT + s"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SHARE_MOM_TOT", 2, "total momentum share of side s, at MOM_TOT + s"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SHARE_EN_OUT", 4, "energy share outside the grid of side s, at EN_OUT + s"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SHARE_EN_TOT", 6, "total energy share of side s, at EN_TOT + s"],
  ["PKPM_RF_SHARE_NUM", 8, "size of share"],
  ["PKPM_RF_NUM_MOMS", 7, "face-frame moments of the flux: M0, M1, M2 of F, M0 of G, M0 of M0_perp (3)"]
]$

/* The body of the loop over the Gauss-Legendre points of the interval kernel: the blocks of both
   sides at the point, the flux, its moments and shares, and its projection onto the cell of each
   side. One call of the flux function, so that it is inlined. */
pkpmRemapFluxIntervalPoint(fh, dir, n) := block([sd, s, k],
  sd : ["l", "r"],
  printf(fh, "    const double wb = mid+ord[g]*half, om = wgt[g]*half; ~%"),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do (
    printf(fh, "    const double eta_~a = cell_~a[0]+cell_~a[1]*wb, leg2_~a = 3.0*eta_~a*eta_~a-1.0; ~%",
      sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s])
  ),
  printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do
    printf(fh, "      X_~a[c] = Y_~a[c]+Y_~a[8+c]*eta_~a+Y_~a[16+c]*leg2_~a; ~%",
      sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s]),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    pkpm_harm_conf_flux(~a, X_l, X_r, wb, fc, 1, phi_l, phi_r, sb); ~%", dir - 1),
  printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      flux[c] = phi_l[c]+phi_r[c]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    mom[0] += om*flux[0]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    mom[1] += om*wb*flux[0]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    mom[2] += om*wb*wb*flux[0]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    mom[3] += om*flux[1]; ~%"),
  for k : 0 thru 2 do printf(fh, "    mom[~a] += om*flux[~a]; ~%", 4 + k, 2 + k),
  printf(fh, "    const double mass = om*fabs(flux[0]); ~%"),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do (
    printf(fh, "    const double w_~a = side_~a[0]*wb+side_~a[1]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    const double cm_~a = side_~a[5]*flux[2]+side_~a[6]*flux[3]+side_~a[7]*flux[4]; ~%",
      sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    const double yf_~a = side_~a[2]*flux[0]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    const double yg_~a = side_~a[3]*(flux[1]-cm_~a+0.5*side_~a[4]*flux[0]); ~%",
      sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    const double mt_~a = mass*fabs(w_~a); ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    const double en_~a = om*(fabs(yf_~a)*w_~a*w_~a+2.0*fabs(yg_~a)); ~%",
      sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    share[~a] += cell_~a[2]*mt_~a; ~%", s - 1, sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    share[~a] += mt_~a; ~%", 2 + s - 1, sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    share[~a] += cell_~a[2]*en_~a; ~%", 4 + s - 1, sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    share[~a] += en_~a; ~%", 6 + s - 1, sd[s])
  ),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do (
    printf(fh, "    const double wt_~a = om*cell_~a[1]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    const double t0_~a = ~a*wt_~a, t1_~a = ~a*wt_~a*eta_~a, t2_~a = ~a*wt_~a*leg2_~a; ~%",
      sd[s], float(n[1]), sd[s], sd[s], float(n[2]), sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], float(n[3]), sd[s], sd[s])
  ),
  printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do (
    printf(fh, "      P_~a[c] += t0_~a*flux[c]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "      P_~a[8+c] += t1_~a*flux[c]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "      P_~a[16+c] += t2_~a*flux[c]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s])
  ),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%")
)$

/* A list of numbers as the C initializer of a double array, each correctly rounded. */
pkpmRemapFluxCList(lst) := block([str, i],
  str : "{",
  for i : 1 thru length(lst) do
    str : sconcat(str, if i > 1 then ", " else "", float(bfloat(lst[i]))),
  sconcat(str, "}")
)$

/* 3-point Gauss-Legendre rule on [-1, 1]. */
pkpmRemapFluxOrds : [-sqrt(3/5), 0, sqrt(3/5)]$
pkpmRemapFluxWgts : [5/9, 8/9, 5/9]$

calcPKPMRemapFluxInterval(dir, fh, funcNm) := block([n],
  /* The factors n of the Legendre modes of the velocity basis, phi_m = n_m [1, eta, 3 eta^2 - 1],
     are printed as the basis constants of the other kernels; the rule correctly rounded, as the
     tables of gkyl_gauss_quad_data.h. */
  n : [1/sqrt(2), sqrt(3/2), sqrt(5/2)/2],
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_remap_flux_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH void ~a(const double *fc, double w_lo, double w_up,
  const double *side_l, const double *side_r, const double *cell_l, const double *cell_r,
  const double *Y_l, const double *Y_r, double* GKYL_RESTRICT P_l, double* GKYL_RESTRICT P_r,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT mom, double* GKYL_RESTRICT share) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // fc:          Face coefficients of the flux at the transverse node (PKPM_FC_*, stride 1). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // w_lo/w_up:   Ends of the interval in the face-frame label. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // side_l/r:    Map of the left/right side to the face frame (PKPM_RF_SIDE_*). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // cell_l/r:    Velocity cell of the left/right side on the interval (PKPM_RF_CELL_*). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // Y_l/Y_r:     Blocks of the left/right side in the face frame, Legendre coefficients in the ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //              cell coordinate of the side: Y[m*8 + c] of [1, eta, 3 eta^2 - 1]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // P_l/P_r:     Accumulated projection of the flux onto the Legendre modes of the cell of the ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //              left/right side, face frame: P[m*8 + c]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // mom:         Accumulated face-frame moments of the flux (PKPM_RF_NUM_MOMS). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // share:       Accumulated shares of the flux for the blend (PKPM_RF_SHARE_*). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // 3-point Gauss-Legendre rule on the interval. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  const double ord[3] = ~a; ~%", pkpmRemapFluxCList(pkpmRemapFluxOrds)),
  printf(fh, "  const double wgt[3] = ~a; ~%", pkpmRemapFluxCList(pkpmRemapFluxWgts)),
  printf(fh, "  const double mid = 0.5*(w_up+w_lo), half = 0.5*(w_up-w_lo); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  double X_l[8], X_r[8], phi_l[8], phi_r[8], flux[8], sb[2]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  for (int g = 0; g < 3; ++g) { ~%"),
  pkpmRemapFluxIntervalPoint(fh, dir, n),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$

/* The factors n of the Legendre modes of the velocity basis, phi_m = n_m [1, eta, 3 eta^2 - 1]. */
pkpmRemapFluxVelNorm : [1/sqrt(2), sqrt(3/2), sqrt(5/2)/2]$

calcPKPMRemapFluxToFace(fh, funcNm, cdim) := block([na, NT, n, m, a],
  na : 2^(cdim - 1), NT : 3*na, n : pkpmRemapFluxVelNorm,
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_remap_flux_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH void ~a(const double *psi, const double *fwd, const double *G,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT X, double* GKYL_RESTRICT Y) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // psi:  Transverse modes at the node. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // fwd:  Factors of the change of frame from the side to the face frame (PKPM_FRAME_*). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // G:    Modal traces of the eight blocks of one velocity cell of the side: ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //       G[c*~a + a*3 + m], a transverse mode, m Legendre mode in w. ~%", NT),
  printf(fh, "  // X:    Output blocks at the node in the frame of the side, Legendre coefficients in w: ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //       X[m*8 + c] of [1, eta, 3 eta^2 - 1]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // Y:    Output blocks at the node in the face frame, Y[m*8 + c]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    const double *g = &G[c*~a]; ~%", NT),
  for m : 0 thru 2 do (
    printf(fh, "    X[~a] = ~a*(", if m = 0 then "c" else sconcat(8*m, "+c"), float(n[m + 1])),
    for a : 0 thru na - 1 do
      printf(fh, "~apsi[~a]*g[~a]", if a > 0 then "+" else "", a, 3*a + m),
    printf(fh, "); ~%")
  ),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  for m : 0 thru 2 do
    printf(fh, "  pkpm_harm_frame_change(&X[~a], fwd, &Y[~a]); ~%", 8*m, 8*m),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$

calcPKPMRemapFluxFromFace(dir, fh, funcNm, cdim) := block(
  [lb, pkC, pkV, pkP, cv, surfCVars, vv, md, tr, bSurf, NK, ipVars, ip, idx, k, a, m, fact],
  lb : loadPKPMPhaseBasis(cdim),
  pkC : copylist(lb[1]), pkV : copylist(lb[3]), pkP : copylist(lb[5]),
  cv : pkC[dir], surfCVars : delete(cv, pkC), vv : pkV[1],
  md : pkpmRemapFluxModes(surfCVars, vv), tr : md[3],
  bSurf : basisFromVars("tenhyb", delete(cv, pkP), 1),
  NK : length(bSurf),
  if NK # length(tr) then error("calcPKPMRemapFluxFromFace: surface basis size mismatch"),
  ipVars : append(surfCVars, [vv]),
  fact : laxFactorizeBasis(bSurf, if cdim > 1 then surfCVars else [prjdummy], pkV),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_remap_flux_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH void ~a(const double *wpsi, const double *bck, const double *P,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT flux) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // wpsi:  Weight of the transverse node times the transverse modes at the node. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // bck:   Factors of the change of frame from the face frame to the side (PKPM_FRAME_*). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // P:     Legendre projections in w of the face-frame flux of the eight blocks on the ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //        velocity cell of the side at the node: P[m*8 + c]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // flux:  Accumulated surface modes of the side of the face: flux[c*~a + k]. ~%", NK),
  printf(fh, "  double Z[24]; ~%"),
  for m : 0 thru 2 do
    printf(fh, "  pkpm_harm_frame_change(&P[~a], bck, &Z[~a]); ~%", 8*m, 8*m),
  printf(fh, "  for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    double *out = &flux[c*~a]; ~%", NK),
  for k : 1 thru NK do (
    ip : calcInnerProdList(ipVars, 1, tr, bSurf[k]),
    idx : sublist_indices(ip, lambda([z], is(abs(float(z) - 1.0) < 1.0e-12))),
    if length(idx) # 1 then error("calcPKPMRemapFluxFromFace: surface mode is not a face mode"),
    a : floor((idx[1] - 1)/3), m : (idx[1] - 1) - 3*a,
    /* As in calcPKPMRemapFluxStore: the stored modes are integrals against the normalized
       shapes of the factorized surface basis, so the store divides by coef_k. */
    printf(fh, "    out[~a] += ~a*wpsi[~a]*Z[~a + c]; ~%", k-1, float(1/fact[3][k]), a, m*8)
  ),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$

calcPKPMRemapFluxLabel(dir, fh, funcNm) := block([ords, wgts, n, sd, s, k],
  ords : pkpmRemapFluxOrds, wgts : pkpmRemapFluxWgts, n : pkpmRemapFluxVelNorm, sd : ["l", "r"],
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_remap_flux_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH void ~a(const double *fc, double w_center, double dw,
  const double *X_l, const double *X_r, double* GKYL_RESTRICT proj, double* GKYL_RESTRICT mom_l,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT mom_r, double* GKYL_RESTRICT speed) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // fc:          Face coefficients of the flux at the transverse node (PKPM_FC_*, stride 1). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // w_center/dw: Center and width of the velocity cell. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // X_l/X_r:     Blocks of the left/right side at the node, each in the frame of its side, ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //              Legendre coefficients in w: X[m*8 + c] of [1, eta, 3 eta^2 - 1]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // proj:        Output projection of the flux onto the Legendre modes of the cell: proj[m*8 + c]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // mom_l/r:     Accumulated moments in w of the contribution of the left/right side ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //              (PKPM_RF_NUM_MOMS). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // speed:       Largest speeds of the flux so far, raised to those of this cell at the node: ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //              [fastest signal in either direction, largest spread of the two bounds]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // 3-point Gauss-Legendre rule on the cell: the ordinates eta, 3 eta^2 - 1 there, and the ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // weights times the Legendre modes of the cell. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  const double eta[3] = ~a; ~%", pkpmRemapFluxCList(ords)),
  printf(fh, "  const double leg2[3] = ~a; ~%", pkpmRemapFluxCList(makelist(3*ords[k]^2 - 1, k, 1, 3))),
  printf(fh, "  const double wgt[3] = ~a; ~%", pkpmRemapFluxCList(wgts)),
  /* weight times the mode at the point: the basis constant n_m times the correctly rounded rest */
  printf(fh, "  const double t0[3] = ~a; ~%",
    pkpmRemapFluxCList(makelist(float(bfloat(wgts[k]))*float(n[1]), k, 1, 3))),
  printf(fh, "  const double t1[3] = ~a; ~%",
    pkpmRemapFluxCList(makelist(float(bfloat(wgts[k]*ords[k]))*float(n[2]), k, 1, 3))),
  printf(fh, "  const double t2[3] = ~a; ~%",
    pkpmRemapFluxCList(makelist(float(bfloat(wgts[k]*(3*ords[k]^2 - 1)))*float(n[3]), k, 1, 3))),
  printf(fh, "  double x_l[8], x_r[8], phi_l[8], phi_r[8], sb[2]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  for (int k = 0; k < 24; ++k) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    proj[k] = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  for (int g = 0; g < 3; ++g) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    const double wq = w_center+0.5*eta[g]*dw, om = 0.5*wgt[g]*dw; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do
    printf(fh, "      x_~a[c] = X_~a[c]+eta[g]*X_~a[8+c]+leg2[g]*X_~a[16+c]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s], sd[s], sd[s]),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    pkpm_harm_conf_flux(~a, x_l, x_r, wq, fc, 1, phi_l, phi_r, sb); ~%", dir - 1),
  printf(fh, "    speed[0] = fmax(speed[0], fmax(-sb[0], sb[1])); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    speed[1] = fmax(speed[1], sb[1]-sb[0]); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      const double flux = phi_l[c]+phi_r[c]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      proj[c] += t0[g]*flux; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      proj[8+c] += t1[g]*flux; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      proj[16+c] += t2[g]*flux; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  for s : 1 thru 2 do (
    printf(fh, "    mom_~a[0] += om*phi_~a[0]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    mom_~a[1] += om*wq*phi_~a[0]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    mom_~a[2] += om*wq*wq*phi_~a[0]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    printf(fh, "    mom_~a[3] += om*phi_~a[1]; ~%", sd[s], sd[s]),
    for k : 0 thru 2 do printf(fh, "    mom_~a[~a] += om*phi_~a[~a]; ~%", sd[s], 4 + k, sd[s], 2 + k)
  ),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$
